Debian package for the llamacpp PHP extension.

`dpkg-buildpackage` builds one module package per PHP version from
`phpquery -V` (`php8.4-llamacpp` on trixie, plucky, and questing,
`php8.5-llamacpp` on resolute) and an empty `php-llamacpp` package that
depends on the default PHP's module. `dh-php` installs:

  /usr/lib/php/<api>/llamacpp.so
  /etc/php/<version>/mods-available/llamacpp.ini

and the maintainer scripts call `php_invoke enmod <version> ALL llamacpp`.
That is the same hook packaged PHP modules use: it registers the module
and enables it for every SAPI of that version (`cli`, `fpm`, `apache2`,
and the rest). A SAPI package installed afterwards enables registered
modules itself, so fpm or apache added later still loads llamacpp.

Build (amd64), after `./scripts/fetch-libllama.sh`:

  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential dpkg-dev debhelper dh-php php-all-dev pkgconf
  ./scripts/release/set-debian-php-package.sh
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

GitHub Actions does this for each suite and appends `+<suite>` to the
Debian version so the packages on the one GitHub Release have distinct
filenames. `scripts/release.sh` tags; it does not build the packages.
